      "why": "Untappd 5.0 (2026-10-15) and Vivino's 2026 rebuild both made personal drink logging worse for long-time users; on the watchlist at 3.55",
      "evidence": "88 low-star reviews in 90d, 87 of them on v5.0.x since 2026-10-16 (us 66, gb 21); before v5 only 1 in 2+ months. Themes: UI/clutter 48, friends feed 17, own history/tracking 12, ads 10, Insider/paywall 7. Kill check: personal beer journals are tiny (Beerstory 0 ratings, Tastings 3, BrewGene 75, Pint Please 35), but Bruwia is free, no subscription, and already imports Untappd history (takeoutday.org guide, 2026-10-15). Untappd's own check-in export is Insider-only (GDPR request in EU). Round 3 added Vivino: ~15 of its 25 low-star reviews (us, gb, Aug–Oct 2026) are about the rebuild breaking manual entry, editing and saved tastings. Off-store searches (round 4) found no Reddit/forum threads, only press about 5.0 (thebeertimes.com, 2026-10-15). 2026-11-03 rescan: Untappd 91 low-star in 90d (us 69, gb 22), now on 5.0.2; Vivino 26 (us 20, gb 6). 2026-11-04 rescan: Untappd 92 in 90d, tapering to 1-6 a day by 10-31, Vivino 27; no new storefronts, no Reddit or forum threads (one more search round). 2026-11-05 daily data: Untappd 92 in 90d, 13 since 10-28; Vivino 27; nothing new off-store. 2026-11-06 daily data: Untappd 92 in 90d, 13 since 10-28, 1 since 11-01; Vivino 27; nothing new off-store. Crumble (free, web, imports Untappd exports) added to the kill check 2026-11-07 daily data: Untappd 91 in 90d, 13 since 10-28, 1 since 11-01; Vivino 27. Kill check grew again: Drinkist (free, no ads, iOS and Android, multi-drink), Brewver (web, imports Untappd ratings) and Taphouse (import and export) are listed in drinkist.app/blog/untappd-alternative (2026-06-26, vendor post) 2026-11-08 daily data: Untappd 91 in 90d, 1 since 11-01 (last scanned 11-04), still v5.0.2",
      "missing": "Decide on the 2026-11-09 recheck: ≥15 low-star on v5.1+ (or Vivino 2026.44+) keeps it; fewer, and it goes to rejected (complaints fading and Drinkist, Bruwia, Crumble, Brewver already serve private logs free). Also still: a storefront beyond us/gb, ≥3 off-store threads, real willingness to pay",
      "rounds": 9,
